  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 200°C. Pulse the chickpeas, onion, garlic, herbs, spices and chickpea flour in a food processor to a coarse, holdable paste. Don't over-blend.",
    "Roll into 16 walnut-sized balls and flatten slightly. Brush all over with olive oil and place on a lined tray.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes, turning halfway, until deeply golden and crisp.",
    "Whisk the tahini with lemon juice and enough cold water to make a pourable, creamy sauce.",
    "Build bowls with couscous, falafel, fresh salad and a generous drizzle of tahini sauce."
  ],
  "notes": "Chill the mix for 20 minutes before shaping if you have time — it firms up and holds together far better in the oven."
}
